cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use SQListo in your research, please cite this software."

title: "SQListo: An AI Assistant for the Storage and Analysis of Molecular Dynamics Trajectories"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Pérez Tabero"
    given-names: "Sergio"
    affiliation: "Universidad Autónoma de Madrid"

version: "0.2.0"

license: MIT

repository-code: "https://github.com/FrustratedAlchemist20/SQListo"

url: "https://github.com/FrustratedAlchemist20/SQListo"

abstract: >
  SQListo is a scientific software platform for the compressed
  storage, retrieval and analysis of molecular dynamics trajectories
  using SQLite databases and a locally deployed artificial
  intelligence assistant. The software integrates molecular
  fragmentation analysis, reaction classification, theoretical
  mass spectrum construction, feature extraction and kinetic
  analysis with natural language database interaction.

keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - computational chemistry
  - theoretical chemistry
  - artificial intelligence
  - large language models
  - SQLite
  - molecular fragmentation
  - mass spectrometry
  - chemical kinetics
  - scientific software
  - TeraChem
  - VENUS

